findings.finding:
The guard test's review-bot scanner may be blind to how real code builds metric data. Its positive self-test runs only on a synthetic module written in the pattern the scanner expects.

As specified, it collects 'each string MetricName passed in a put_metric_data call'. That misses:
- MetricData lists or dicts built before the call (e.g. in a loop, as token-usage metrics likely are);
- names held in module-level constants;
- overlaps where a review-bot f-string prefix matches a probe name, if 'intersection' means set equality.
